  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN232.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">tōḻi talaimakaṉ ciṟaippuṟattāṉākat talaimaṭkuc colluvāḷāyc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the confidante said as one who is speaking to HER while HE was behind the hedge.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN232.1">
        <l>kāṇiṉi vāḻi tōḻi pāṉāḷ</l>
        <l>maḻaimuḻaṅ <supplied>kara</supplied>vaṅ kēṭṭa kaḻaitiṉ</l>
        <l>mā<supplied>a</supplied>l yāṉai pulicettu verīi</l>
        <l>yiruṅkal viṭarakañ cilampap peytikum</l>
        <l>peruṅka ṉāṭaṉ kēṇmai yiṉiyē</l>
        <l>kuṉṟa vēlic ciṟukuṭi yāṅkaṇ</l>
        <l>maṉṟa vēṅkai maṇanāṭ pūtta</l>
        <l>maṇiyē rarumpiṉ poṉvī tāay</l>
        <l>viyalaṟai varikku muṉṟiṟ ku<supplied>ṟa</supplied>var</l>
        <l>maṉaimutir makaḷiroṭu kuravai tūṅku</l>
        <l>mārkali viḻavukkaḷaṅ kaṭuppa nāḷum</l>
        <l>viravuppūm paliyoṭu<anchor n="1"/> viraii yaṉṉai</l>
        <l>kaṭiyuṭai viyaṉakark kāvaṟ kaṇṇi</l>
        <l>murukaṉ vēlaṟ ṟarūum</l>
        <l>paruva mākap payantaṉṟā ṉamakkē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1a-c">See now, oh friend:</l>
        <l corresp="5a-c">the intimacy with the man from a land of big stones,</l>
        <l>where at midnight rain pours down so that it echoes inside dark stone caves,</l>
        <l>a the bamboo-eating huge elephant that heard the thundering sound,</l>
        <l corresp="1d-4">thinks [it that of] the tiger [and] is frightened,</l>
        <l rend="indent8" corresp="5d">now</l>
        <l corresp="15">it has borne fruit for us as the occasion</l>
        <l corresp="13">when mother, mixing assorted flowers with offerings</l>
        <l corresp="11">daily, so that [the yard?] resembles a bustling festival floor,</l>
        <l corresp="9">where the hill people in the front-yard lined out in the wide rocks</l>
        <l corresp="10">sway in the Kuravai with the mature women of the house,</l>
        <l corresp="8">as golden blossoms spread from the jewel-like buds</l>
        <l corresp="7">that flowered on a day of union on the kino tree of the village common,</l>
        <l corresp="6">there in the small hamlet fenced by the hills,</l>
        <l corresp="14">brings Murukaṉ’s spear[-bear]er</l>
        <l corresp="13">with a chaplet for guarding the protected wide mansion.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

